ArcPy-generated string formats badly in map text element
I've got a script that's pulling a bunch of attributes and concatenating the information into a long string. text_description = "Address: {}

".format(dictADDR[key]) text_description += "{} Customers.".format(len(listCustomer)) if countPole == 0: text_description += "No Poles
" else: text_description += "Poles:
" text_description += " Pole Quantity: {}
".format(countPole) (et cetera) The goal is to include this string both in an emailed final report when the script finishes, and include it in a text element on a PDF map (displayed next to the parcel and an aerial map). This works fine for the email, and gives something like: Address: 1225 BICKLEY RD 0 Customers No Poles No Overhead Distribution However, in the text element it ends up ignoring spacing and overlaps some text with other text (see image below). Copy-pasting the contents of the text properties box, it appears to have the line breaks in the correct places: Address: 1225 BICKLEY RD 0 Customers. No Poles No Electric Overhead Distribution What's going wrong, and what should I change in either the text element or my code to fix it?

